---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { manifestEntry } from '../lib/seo/pages.ts';
const path = '/disclaimer/';
const entry = manifestEntry(path);
---

<BaseLayout
  title={entry?.title ?? ''}
  description={entry?.description ?? ''}
  path={path}
  indexable={entry?.indexable ?? false}
  crumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
    { name: 'Disclaimer', path },
  ]}
>
  <h1>Disclaimer</h1>

  <div class="notice notice--warning">
    <p class="notice__title">These are estimates, not advice</p>
    <p style="margin-bottom:0;">
      Nothing on this site is tax, legal, mortgage, or financial advice. No tax professional has
      reviewed it.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>What the figures assume</h2>
  <p>
    Every result assumes one ordinary employment profile held for a whole tax year, with a standard
    tax code and no unusual circumstances. The full list of assumptions appears next to every
    result, and it is worth reading — most differences between our figure and your payslip come from
    one of them.
  </p>

  <h2>Why your payslip may differ</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Payroll withholds period by period; we annualise. A mid-year start or salary change produces
      different monthly figures.
    </li>
    <li>
      Your tax code may not be the standard one. Codes are issued individually and we do not model
      them.
    </li>
    <li>
      Benefits in kind, salary sacrifice arrangements, multiple jobs, and other income are not
      included.
    </li>
    <li>
      Some contributions stop mid-year once an annual maximum is reached, changing individual pay
      periods.
    </li>
    <li>Your circumstances may fall outside the supported profile entirely.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Mortgage figures</h2>
  <p>
    The mortgage tools are arithmetic. They do not assess affordability, do not indicate whether any
    lender would lend to you, and exclude fees, insurance, and early repayment charges. They assume
    one fixed rate for the whole term, which is not how most mortgages work.
  </p>

  <h2>If a figure looks wrong</h2>
  <p>
    Check the assumptions on the page, then the official source linked beneath it. If you still
    think it is wrong, please <a href="/corrections/">tell us</a> — we would rather fix it than have it
    stand.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
